<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Huế (1884)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1884</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Patenôtre Treaty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1883">Treaty of Huế</a> of 6 June 1884, negotiated by the French diplomat Jules Patenôtre, confirmed French protection over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> after the conquest of Tonkin. It replaced the harsher Harmand Treaty of 1883, leaving Annam under the Nguyễn emperor with French oversight and placing Tonkin under closer French control. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> accepted the arrangement in 1885 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1884.jpg" alt="Treaty of Huế (1884)" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jules Patenôtre des Noyers (20 April 1845 – 26 December 1925). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%E1%BA%A3n_sao_Trang_cu%E1%BB%91i_c%E1%BB%A7a_Hi%E1%BB%87p_%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Bc_Paten%C3%B4tre_(6-6-1884)_c%C3%B3_ch%E1%BB%AF_k%C3%BD_c%E1%BB%A7a_Paten%C3%B4tre_-_%C4%91%E1%BA%A1i_di%E1%BB%87n_n%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Bc_Ph%C3%A1p_v%C3%A0_c%C3%A1c_quan_%C4%91%E1%BA%A1i_th%E1%BA%A7n_%C4%90%E1%BA%A1i_Nam_Nguy%E1%BB%85n_V%C4%83n_T%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Dng,_Ph%E1%BA%A1m_Th%E1%BA%ADn_Du%E1%BA%ADt_v%C3%A0_T%C3%B4n_Th%E1%BA%A5t_Phan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
